{
	quest.0DBA62B3DF059DAA.title: "<scrare>Rare</scrare>"
	quest.0ECAE877F6701A19.quest_desc: ["Displays all of the previous equipment's information as a single item."]
	quest.116F4BBCDE70B6DA.quest_desc: ["Gives you a double jump when equipped that is restored upon landing."]
	quest.1418C2DE3A0BD05B.quest_desc: ["Some of the trash might still be useful however, so don't throw them away immediately."]
	quest.1418C2DE3A0BD05B.quest_subtitle: "Not all of them can be winners..."
	quest.1418C2DE3A0BD05B.title: "<sctrash>Trash</sctrash>"
	quest.17697AD359B82027.quest_desc: ["Sometimes, you might fish up a &6crate&r instead of a fish. These crates may contain (&#57C47ETide&r) fish related loot when placed down."]
	quest.17697AD359B82027.title: "Crates"
	quest.18AF11596AF302E5.quest_desc: ["You can obviously fish in water, but... there are other fluids you can fish in."]
	quest.18AF11596AF302E5.quest_subtitle: "Well, duh..."
	quest.18AF11596AF302E5.title: "Water"
	quest.1987C488C9637C0B.quest_desc: [
		"&6Baits&r affect how fast a fish bites and what type of fish bite. Some fishes even require specific baits to even be fished up in the first place!"
		""
		"&6Worms&r make for a good bait. You can try gathering some by &bbone mealing farmland&r."
		""
		"You can also use &ebuckets&r as bait. It doesn't increase any chances or anything, but puts whatever you fish up inside of the bucket, provided it has a bucket variant."
	]
	quest.1987C488C9637C0B.title: "Baits"
	quest.1ADC9152B4DF89BC.quest_desc: ["The &6Tournament Stand&r allows you to host fishing tournaments where you can compete with other players by trying to fish the most amount of fishes in a given duration."]
	quest.1B0E8F0403672571.quest_desc: [
		"Very rarely, you may fish a <scgolden>golden</scgolden> variant of a fish. These are just a golden recolor of the existing fish that you can only fish up <pulse frequency=2 colors=\"\">ONCE</pulse>."
		""
		"&8<wiggle amplitude=0.2>Due to limitations, this quest can't auto track whenever you fish a <scgolden>golden</scgolden> fish, so only check off this quest when you actually fish one up. Thank you.</wiggle>&r"
	]
	quest.1B0E8F0403672571.title: "<scgolden>Golden</scgolden>"
	quest.2253D90ED35A96D1.quest_desc: [
		"&#F81A45Starcatcher&r adds custom templates that allow you to customize your rod's appearance. There are two types: &6Tackle Templates&r and &6Skin Templates&r."
		""
		"&6Tackle Template&r change the appearance of the rod's bobber. Some of them even have custom sound effects."
		""
		"&6Skin Templates&r modify the appearance of the rod in your hand."
		""
		"These changes are purely cosmetic and don't give you any advantages, other than bragging right. They can be rarely fished up while fishing."
	]
	quest.2253D90ED35A96D1.title: "Templates"
	quest.22572D0319706BB1.quest_desc: [
		"When you cast your &dStarcatcher's Rod&r, a fish might bite after a while. Once one bites, you can reel it in. Reeling it in won't be easy tho, as you will need a minigame to be able to reel in the fish."
		""
		"The minigame is fairly simple, press Space (or right click) whenever the handle is above a &#ADDF81sweetspot&r. Hitting sweetspots will cause the fish to be reeled up and missing will obviously cause it to down. The reel is successful when the fish reaches the very top and, likewise, fails when it reaches the bottom, leaving you with nothing."
		""
		"Each fish is different and so will be the minigame. This means each fish will have different amount of &#ADDF81sweetspots&r, &#81DFC2sweetspot types&r, &9speed&r, &cpenalties&r and much more."
	]
	quest.22572D0319706BB1.title: "The Minigame"
	quest.25E14AB6303B2C99.title: "<scuncommon>Uncommon</scuncommon>"
	quest.2ADE33210012686B.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Fish Satchel&r is basically a fish version of a bundle. It can hold up to a stack of different fish."
		""
		"When right clicked, you can toggle it between opened and closed. While opened, any fish that enter your inventory will be immediately put into the &6Satchel&r."
	]
	quest.2B5A3BF64E037883.quest_desc: ["&6Hats&r are simple cosmetic items that can be found in shipwrecks. Some of them might have bonus for the minigame."]
	quest.3226BCDEBF62A18B.quest_desc: [
		"A more unique fishing spot is the <pulse colors=\"#440077\"><shake frequency=2>VOID</shake></pulse>."
		""
		"You will need a &eCloud Bobber&r again to achieve this though so the bobber just doesn't fall into the void."
		""
		"Then you'll need to find a suitable spot to even reach the void..."
		"Some places are easier to get to the void than others..."
		""
		"Maybe there's something you can fish up to help you break the bedrock in the Overworld?"
	]
	quest.3226BCDEBF62A18B.title: "Void"
	quest.33219C53FFC750C6.quest_desc: [
		"&#F81A45Starcatcher&r allows you to fish in lava as well!"
		""
		"A flimsy rod won't do though, you will either need to replace your hook with an &eAmethyst Hook&r or upgrade your rod with netherite."
	]
	quest.33219C53FFC750C6.title: "Lava"
	quest.36AF82A5B80C18A7.quest_desc: [
		"&6Tackle Boxes&r serve two purposes."
		""
		"First, they allow you to store all of your fishing related items, even having a specific slot for all of the fishes you catch."
		""
		"Second, they allow you to modify your Starcatcher's Rod's bobber, hook and bait. Changing those will make the minigame easier (or even harder in some cases). This can be helpful if you're having trouble fishing up a specific fish."
	]
	quest.36EBD9F6447B4BCC.title: "<sccommon>Common</sccommon>"
	quest.3CD7822A3F293D84.quest_desc: [
		"&6Bobbers&r mainly modifies the sweetspots in a minigame."
		""
		"[ \"They don't change the appearance of the bobber however. You need \", { \"text\": \"Tackle Templates\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"change_page\", \"value\": \"2253D90ED35A96D1\" } }, \" for that.\" ]"
		""
		"Don't be afraid to use them to make fishing easier. It's even recommended to use them as some fishes might be impossible to even reel in without them..."
	]
	quest.3CD7822A3F293D84.title: "Bobbers"
	quest.4342F4E3C85029E1.quest_desc: ["&6Hooks&r mainly modify where you can fish, the things you're able to reel in and the handle inside of the minigame."]
	quest.4342F4E3C85029E1.title: "Hooks"
	quest.46191333D6C9AFA9.title: "<scepic>Epic</scepic>"
	quest.4818F435EBEEEFE0.quest_desc: [
		"You did the impossible..."
		""
		"Not only did you catch every <sccommon>common</sccommon>, <scuncommon>uncommon</scuncommon>, <scrare>rare</scrare>, <scepic>epic</scepic> and <sclegendary>legendary</sclegendary> fish, but you also caught every fish in their <scgolden>golden</scgolden> variant."
	]
	quest.4818F435EBEEEFE0.title: "Trophy Of The Older Angler"
	quest.48575FBE3463668F.quest_desc: [
		"If you catch a certain amount of fishes, you might get rewarded with a &6trophy&r on your next reel! These &6trophies&r scale in difficulty the rarer the material is."
		""
		"Next page contains information on how to get every trophy in the mod."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The &#FF7C29Copper Trophy&r is reeled in after <obfuscate mode=\"REVEAL\" interval=200 direction=\"RANDOM\">catching 25 common fishes</obfuscate>."
		""
		"The &#C3C3C3Iron Trophy&r is reeled in after <obfuscate mode=\"REVEAL\" interval=200 direction=\"RANDOM\">catching 35 unique fishes</obfuscate>."
		""
		"The &#FFB633Gold Trophy&r is reeled in after <obfuscate mode=\"REVEAL\" interval=200 direction=\"RANDOM\">catching 100 fishes, 2 unique <sclegendary>legendary</sclegendary> fishes and 2 unique <scgolden>golden</scgolden> fishes</obfuscate>."
		""
		"The &#82FF4CEmerald Trophy&r is reeled in after <obfuscate mode=\"REVEAL\" interval=200 direction=\"RANDOM\">catching 200 fishes and 10 unique <sclegendary>legendary</sclegendary> fishes</obfuscate>."
		""
		"The &#69EBFFDiamond Trophy&r is reeled in after <obfuscate mode=\"REVEAL\" interval=200 direction=\"RANDOM\">catching 500 total fishes and catching every fish in the pack</obfuscate>."
	]
	quest.48575FBE3463668F.title: "Trophies"
	quest.554DCAB20E2F6B63.quest_desc: ["Displays when the next rain or thunderstorm is to nearby players when placed down."]
	quest.563952EE112F496D.quest_desc: ["Shoots out a special type of arrow that isn't affected by gravity."]
	quest.57AD878022EEBA60.quest_desc: [
		"Oh, hey! A <shiny>shiny</shiny> one!"
		""
		"..."
		""
		"&7<shake amplitude=0.2 frequency=0.5>What a shame...</shake>&r"
	]
	quest.57AD878022EEBA60.title: "<shiny>Shiny</shiny> Pokémon"
	quest.59D7F279BB93F97E.quest_desc: [
		"&6Aquariums&r are fun way to display the fish you have caught, without having the need to worry about your fish swimming off or dying."
		""
		"First, get a live fish in a &ebucket&r by &busing a bucket as bait&r. Then you can just right click the aquarium with the bucket containing the fish to put the fish into the aquarium. If you want to get the fish out at some point, simply right click the aquarium with an &eempty bucket&r."
		""
		"You can further decorate the aquarium by replacing the ground with &eSand&r, &eRed Sand&r, &eStone&r or &eGravel&r. You can even form a sand castle by using a &eshovel&r on the sand blocks or a small caverns by using a &epickaxe&r on stone. &eSeagrass&r, &eKelp&r, &eClams&r and &eConches&r can also be added to an &6aquarium&r."
	]
	quest.5C5E7C278D38B14A.quest_desc: ["The sky's the limit on where you can fish, literally! You are able to fish in the sky thanks to the &6Cloud Bobber&r, which removes gravity from your bobber, allowing you to fish in the sky."]
	quest.5C5E7C278D38B14A.title: "Sky"
	quest.5E4B0D0A4CE4AE15.quest_desc: [""]
	quest.6747251CA862F7ED.quest_desc: [
		"A powerful &6watch&r that is able to freeze mobs in time, basically rendering them almost like as if they have no AI."
		""
		"Right click a frozen mob again to unfreeze them."
	]
	quest.696F4F5ED720AF29.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Fish Display&r and the &6Starcatcher's Display&r can be used to display your most prized fish. Keep in mind though that the &6Fish Display&r is only able to display fishes from &#57C47ETide 2&r and the &6Starcatcher's Display&r only those from &#F81A45Starcatcher&r."
		""
		"&6Starcatcher's Display&r is also able to display the &eStarcatcher's Guide&r."
	]
	quest.696F4F5ED720AF29.title: "Display"
	quest.700681B41AC68176.quest_desc: [
		"Oh, hey. You just fished up a Pokémon!"
		""
		"..."
		""
		"&7<shake amplitude=0.2 frequency=0.5>Is it alive...?</shake>&r"
	]
	quest.72122E04B9E267BC.title: "<sclegendary>Legendary</sclegendary>"
	quest.7AD365D9339DBD90.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Starcatcher's Guide&r is the guide book for the entire mod. It contains information on how to play the mod, as well as every fish you have encountered and can encounter. It's worth taking a look inside!"
		""
		"Flipping the book all the way to the left will allow you to &esign it&r, remembering whatever progress you currently have so you can show your friends the master fisher that you are! Keep in mind that this process is irrevesible, meaning you will need to craft a new &6Guide&r, if you want it to track progress again. Also keep in mind that you don't need to always have the &6Guide&r on you to track progress in the first place."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The &6Fishing Journal&r is &#57C47ETide 2&r's book. It contains a list of every fish in &#57C47ETide 2&r."
		""
		"Normally, you are only able to fill in the &6Journal&r by fishing up the respective fish using one of &#57C47ETide&r's fishing rod, but those have been disabled. Instead, you can record a valid fish by holding in your off-hand and then right clicking with the &6Journal&r in your main hand."
	]
	quest.7AD365D9339DBD90.quest_subtitle: "Fishing 4 Dummies"
	quest.7AF1055789B1BB86.quest_desc: ["The &6Fish Radar&r is a simple tool that shows the fish you are able to catch around you."]
	quest.7BC2D59B27F34BC8.quest_desc: [
		"&#F81A45Starcatcher&r is a mod that completely revamps fishing! It adds a brand new fishing minigame, a whole lot of new fishes that come with different lengths and weights and even trophies. Thanks to &#57C47ETide 2&r, there are even more fishes to be caught."
		""
		"To get started, you first need to craft a &dStarcatcher's Rod&r as the vanilla fishing rod has stayed untouched."
	]
	task.032540C1360ECF17.title: "Unknown Fish"
	task.128C3705857C50DD.title: "Shiny Pokémon"
	task.1F95DB34CDBF92D4.title: "Skin Template"
	task.210B75371A281529.title: "Bobber"
	task.22D2E33402B8B047.title: "Tackle Template"
	task.2DD349B71463D2DD.title: "Hook"
	task.354F2417290A6B35.title: "Netherite items"
	task.59B8BB32063B5F84.title: "Bait"
	task.6CEA7CFD846C7F40.title: "Pokémon"
}
